# Desktop Architecture (Electron)

Scribely desktop is a macOS-only Electron overlay app. It floats above all windows, is invisible to screen sharing, and provides live transcription (local Whisper), AI chat, and real-time insights.

## File Organization

```
desktop/
├── src/
│   ├── main/                   # Main process (Node.js)
│   │   ├── index.ts            # Entry: window, IPC registration, lifecycle
│   │   ├── hotkey.ts           # Global hotkeys (Alt+T, Alt+M)
│   │   ├── invisibility.ts     # NSWindow screen-share hiding
│   │   ├── ws-server.ts        # WebSocket server (port 9876) for Chrome extension
│   │   ├── native-bridge.ts    # Unix socket → Swift NativeHelper
│   │   ├── screen-recorder.ts  # ScreenCaptureKit
│   │   ├── audio/              # Audio pipeline
│   │   │   ├── pipeline.ts     # VAD + Whisper + frame routing
│   │   │   ├── transcriber.ts  # Local Whisper
│   │   │   └── vad.ts
│   │   ├── llm/                # OpenAI SDK (direct, not OpenRouter)
│   │   │   ├── llm-service.ts   # Chat, streaming, system prompts
│   │   │   ├── prompt-assembler.ts
│   │   │   └── background-summarizer.ts
│   │   └── insights/           # Live Insights
│   │       ├── insight-engine.ts
│   │       └── heuristic-detector.ts
│   ├── preload/index.ts        # contextBridge → ElectronAPI
│   └── renderer/src/           # React 18 frontend
│       ├── components/          # Overlay, LiveTranscriptPanel, InputBar, etc.
│       ├── hooks/               # useChat, useAudioCapture, useMeetingTranscript
│       ├── types/               # ElectronAPI, settings, transcript
│       └── themes/              # Theme registry
├── native/                     # Swift NativeHelper (ScreenCaptureKit)
└── package.json
```

## Three-Process Model

| Process | Role |
|---------|------|
| **Main** | Owns AudioPipeline, LLMService, InsightEngine, ExtensionWsServer, electron-store, hotkeys |
| **Preload** | Secure bridge via `contextBridge`; exposes `window.electronAPI` |
| **Renderer** | React UI; all data via `window.electronAPI` |

## IPC Patterns

| Pattern | Direction | Example |
|---------|------------|---------|
| `invoke` | renderer → main → renderer | `llm:set-model`, `meeting:start-session` |
| `send` | renderer → main | `llm:chat`, `update-settings`, `meeting:audio-frame` |
| `on` | main → renderer | `llm:chat-delta`, `meeting:transcript-entry`, `insight:new` |

**Adding a new IPC channel**: Update `main/index.ts`, `preload/index.ts`, and `renderer/src/types/index.ts`.

## Audio Pipeline

Three capture modes (priority: extension > native > browser):
1. **Extension** — Chrome extension streams 16kHz PCM over WebSocket
2. **Native** — Swift NativeHelper (ScreenCaptureKit) + mic via getUserMedia
3. **Browser** — getUserMedia + getDisplayMedia fallback

Flow: PCM → resample 16kHz → energy gate → 2s chunks → Whisper → transcript entry → renderer

## Commands

```bash
npm run dev          # Dev with HMR
npm run build        # Build main + preload + renderer
npm run build:native # Build Swift NativeHelper
npm run typecheck
```
